---
import MockComposer from './app/MockComposer.astro';
import LedgerRow from './LedgerRow.astro';
import SplitSection from './SplitSection.astro';

// The hosts the repo's own live checks pass against, IMAP on 993 and SMTP on 465 both
// (packages/imap and packages/smtp `live`): keep this list equal to theirs.
const providers = [
  'Gmail',
  'Fastmail',
  'Forward Email',
  'Gandi',
  'Disroot',
  'mailbox.org',
  'Riseup',
  'Migadu',
  'Posteo',
];
---

<SplitSection
  id="send"
  label="01 · Send-as"
  title={'Gmail stops sending as your domain in January\u00a02027.'}
>
  <p>If you write as <span class="code">you@yourdomain.com</span> from inside Gmail, that ends.</p>
  <p>
    In YOZZ it is the normal case. Add as many addresses as you own, each with the SMTP server you
    already use, and pick From on every message. An address with no inbox behind it is fine too.
  </p>
  <ol class="dates">
    <LedgerRow label="Jan 2026">Gmail removed POP fetch and Gmailify.</LedgerRow>
    <LedgerRow label="Jan 2027">Gmail removes “Send mail as” for third-party addresses.</LedgerRow>
    <LedgerRow label="In YOZZ" isEmphasised>
      No limit on addresses. Each one sends over its own SMTP.
    </LedgerRow>
  </ol>

  <figure slot="aside">
    <MockComposer />
    <figcaption class="caption">
      <span>Demo addresses. Nothing is sent from this page.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ul class="providers" slot="below">
    <LedgerRow label="Connects to">
      {providers.join(', ')}. Gmail connects with an app password. We test the encrypted
      connection to all nine, and signing in and sending on one. Any server with IMAP on port 993
      and SMTP on port 465 should work too.
    </LedgerRow>
    <LedgerRow label="Not yet">
      Providers that need OAuth sign-in, or that only offer SMTP on port 587.
    </LedgerRow>
  </ul>
</SplitSection>

<style>
  .dates {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  /* A row of its own under the copy and the composer, so neither column runs past the other. It
     keeps the split's own columns and gap (SplitSection): "Not yet" sits under the copy, and the
     longer "Connects to" under the composer. */
  .providers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    column-gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 96px);
    margin-top: 56px;
  }

  .providers :global(.row:first-child) {
    order: 1;
  }

  .providers :global(.row) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .providers {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .providers :global(.row:first-child) {
      order: 0;
    }

    .providers :global(.row:not(:first-child)) {
      border-top: 0;
    }

    .providers :global(.value) {
      max-width: 36em;
    }
  }
</style>
